# A shard root activation of the purged incarnation keeps admitting writes after
# the purge, stamping them with the generation it now reads, instead of refusing
# operations on a deleted tree before any routing-generation work. Once the
# re-created incarnation has initialised, that generation is the re-created one,
# loaded at L's partition, so the write is allocated above the recorded close.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitAdmitAfterPurge
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a deleted tree's shard root keeps admitting writes after the purge
PERTURBS: Admit

--- FIND
    /\ ~recreated
    /\ live[i]
    /\ ~pend[i]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no deleted-tree refusal before the stamp is taken.
    /\ ~pend[i]
--- END
